# Dual remotes (dev + production)

When this project has **two** GitHub remotes, keep them in sync on every ship.

| Remote | URL | Role |
|--------|-----|------|
| `origin` | `https://github.com/diasbek/next-metric.git` | Personal / working copy |
| `minim` | `https://github.com/minimdesigngroup/next-metric.git` | **Production** (client org) — if used |

## When the user asks to commit and push

1. Create **one** commit locally as usual (do not duplicate commits).
2. If both remotes exist, push **in parallel** to both:

```bash
git push origin HEAD &
git push minim HEAD &
wait
```

3. Report both push results (or one failure clearly).
4. Do **not** push only to one remote unless the user explicitly says so.
5. Never force-push unless the user explicitly requests it.
